uxlfoundation/oneTBB @ 8976636cbd89 (master, 2026-09-23): derive the external
thread's stack size from emscripten's real stack bounds.

picovoxel, an unofficial community TypeScript/WebAssembly binding of LEAP 71's
PicoGK, applies the same code change to its vendored oneTBB as the second hunk
of patches/oneTBB/0001-wasm-substrate-edges.patch. That file does not apply to
master (its Clang.cmake hunk lost its context), so this file carries the same
code regenerated for master, with the comment reworded.

The defect. get_stack_attributes' EMSCRIPTEN branch (src/tbb/governor.cpp:180-181)
sets only stack_base, so stack_size keeps its fallback, the worker stack size.
The external thread runs on -sSTACK_SIZE (8 MB by default), so its stealing
threshold (base - size/2) is derived from the wrong stack, and it stops stealing
once it is worker_stack_size/2 deep in its own, much larger stack.

The fix: stack_size = stack_base - emscripten_stack_get_end().

Output values: none; this changes which thread runs a task, not what the task
computes.

Measured (picovoxel, emscripten 5.0.1, Apple M2 Pro, 2026-07-26): at 72 KB of
recursion depth, the external thread's task share went from 0.71x to 0.98x of
its share at shallow depth, and it could steal again. All 12 threads took part
before and after; the loss was in share, not participation.

Applies with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0` at the root of a oneTBB master checkout.
Independent of the other two oneTBB proposals.
Not applied by picovoxel's build; see upstream/README.md.

--- a/src/tbb/governor.cpp
+++ b/src/tbb/governor.cpp
@@ -179,6 +179,13 @@
     stack_base = reinterpret_cast<std::uintptr_t>(pteb->StackBase);
 #elif defined(EMSCRIPTEN)
     stack_base = reinterpret_cast<std::uintptr_t>(emscripten_stack_get_base());
+    // Emscripten knows the calling thread's real stack bounds, so fill in the
+    // size as well instead of keeping the fallback. The fallback is the worker
+    // stack size, but the external thread runs on -sSTACK_SIZE (8 MB by
+    // default), so the stealing threshold (base - size/2) was derived from the
+    // wrong stack and the external thread stopped stealing once it was
+    // worker_stack_size/2 deep in its own, much larger stack.
+    stack_size = stack_base - reinterpret_cast<std::uintptr_t>(emscripten_stack_get_end());
 #else
     // There is no portable way to get stack base address in Posix, so we use
     // non-portable method (on all modern Linux) or the simplified approach
